  "question": {
    "text": "In an AC circuit, the instantaneous values of&nbsp;<strong>emf</strong> and current are&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ε</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>200</mn><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>300</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></mrow></mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>sin</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>300</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">π</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>&nbsp;respectively. The average power consumed (in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>watt</mi></math>) is",
